&gt; [DATE], the Warriors had a mystery on their hands. Team trainers were noticing that the stationary bikes in their practice facility had become rather unstationary. More to the point, they were disappearing. Eventually, the mystery was solved. Green was dragging the stationary cycles to the sauna and leaving them there to soak.
&gt; 
&gt; It turned out that [ORGANIZATION], who's struggled with his weight since [DATE] at [LOCATION], had developed a theory: By riding the bikes in the sauna, he could more efficiently shed pounds. In the short term, biking in a sauna will do that, but much of what is lost is water weight and is soon gained back. [ORGANIZATION] trainers were aware that [ORGANIZATION]'s regimen was, at best, scientifically dubious. Also, the bikes were getting ruined. Says a former [ORGANIZATION] trainer: "He would come in and say, 'The screen's not working on the bike.' And I'd be like, 'Yeah, I wonder why.'"
&gt; 
&gt; Still, the team chose to ultimately allow it. It did involve cardio. And [PERSON] was loath to give it up. At [DATE], success trusts its routine, no matter how absurd, grueling or dangerous to electronic equipment it might be.

